#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1735
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"How to set an environment variable differs between shells.  In man:tcsh[1] "
"and man:csh[1], use `setenv` to set environment variables.  In man:sh[1] and "
"`bash`, use `export` to set the current environment variables.  This example "
"sets the default `EDITOR` to `/usr/local/bin/emacs` for the man:tcsh[1] "
"shell:"
msgstr "不同 shell 设置环境变量的方式不同。在 man:tcsh[1] 和 man:csh[1] 中，使用 `setenv` 设置环境变量。在 man:sh[1] 和 `bash` 中，使用 `export` 设置当前环境变量。以下示例为 man:tcsh[1] shell 将默认的 `EDITOR` 设置为 `/usr/local/bin/emacs`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1739
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% setenv EDITOR /usr/local/bin/emacs\n"
msgstr "% setenv EDITOR /usr/local/bin/emacs\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1742
#, fuzzy
msgid "The equivalent command for `bash` would be:"
msgstr "`bash` 中的等效命令如下："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1746
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% export EDITOR=\"/usr/local/bin/emacs\"\n"
msgstr "% export EDITOR=\"/usr/local/bin/emacs\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1750
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To expand an environment variable in order to see its current setting, type "
"a `$` character in front of its name on the command line.  For example, "
"`echo $TERM` displays the current `$TERM` setting."
msgstr "要展开环境变量并查看其当前设置，请在命令行中的变量名称前输入 `$` 字符。例如，`echo $TERM` 会显示当前的 `$TERM` 设置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1755
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Shells treat special characters, known as meta-characters, as special "
"representations of data.  The most common meta-character is `\\*`, which "
"represents any number of characters in a filename.  Meta-characters can be "
"used to perform filename globbing.  For example, `echo *` is equivalent to "
"`ls` because the shell takes all the files that match `*` and `echo` lists "
"them on the command line."
msgstr "Shell 会将称为元字符的特殊字符视为数据的特殊表示。最常见的元字符是 `\\*`，它表示文件名中的任意数量字符。元字符可用于文件名通配。例如，`echo *` 等效于 `ls`，因为 shell 会将所有匹配 `*` 的文件传给 `echo`，由它在命令行中列出这些文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1758
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To prevent the shell from interpreting a special character, escape it from "
"the shell by starting it with a backslash (`\\`).  For example, `echo $TERM` "
"prints the terminal setting whereas `echo \\$TERM` literally prints the "
"string `$TERM`."
msgstr "要阻止 shell 解释特殊字符，请在其前面加上反斜杠（`\\`）对其进行转义。例如，`echo $TERM` 会打印终端设置，而 `echo \\$TERM` 会原样打印字符串 `$TERM`。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1760
#, no-wrap
msgid "Changing the Shell"
msgstr "切换 Shell"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1765
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The easiest way to permanently change the default shell is to use `chsh`.  "
"Running this command will open the editor that is configured in the `EDITOR` "
"environment variable, which by default is set to man:vi[1].  Change the "
"`Shell:` line to the full path of the new shell."
msgstr "永久更改默认 shell 最简单的方法是使用 `chsh`。运行此命令会打开由 `EDITOR` 环境变量指定的编辑器，该变量默认设置为 man:vi[1]。将 `Shell:` 行更改为新 shell 的完整路径。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1768
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Alternately, use `chsh -s` which will set the specified shell without "
"opening an editor.  For example, to change the shell to `bash`:"
msgstr "也可以使用 `chsh -s` 设置指定的 shell，而不打开编辑器。例如，要将 shell 更改为 `bash`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1772
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% chsh -s /usr/local/bin/bash\n"
msgstr "% chsh -s /usr/local/bin/bash\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1776
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Enter the password at the prompt and press kbd:[Return] to change the "
"shell.  Log off and log in again to start using the new shell."
msgstr "在提示时输入密码，然后按 kbd:[Return] 更改 shell。注销后重新登录即可开始使用新的 shell。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1782
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The new shell _must_ be present in `/etc/shells`.  If the shell was "
"installed from the FreeBSD Ports Collection as described in crossref:"
"ports[ports,Installing Applications: Packages and Ports], it should be "
"automatically added to this file.  If it is missing, add it using this "
"command, replacing the path with the path of the shell:"
msgstr "新 shell __必须__存在于 `/etc/shells` 中。如果 shell 是按照 crossref:ports[ports,Installing Applications: Packages and Ports] 中的说明从 FreeBSD Ports Collection 安装的，它应该会自动添加到此文件中。如果缺少该条目，请使用以下命令添加，并将路径替换为 shell 的路径："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1786
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# echo /usr/local/bin/bash >> /etc/shells\n"
msgstr "# echo /usr/local/bin/bash >> /etc/shells\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1789
#, fuzzy
msgid "Then, rerun man:chsh[1]."
msgstr "然后重新运行 man:chsh[1]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1791
#, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced Shell Techniques"
msgstr "高级 Shell 使用技巧"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1795
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The UNIX(R) shell is not just a command interpreter, it acts as a powerful "
"tool which allows users to execute commands, redirect their output, redirect "
"their input and chain commands together to improve the final command "
"output.  When this functionality is mixed with built in commands, the user "
"is provided with an environment that can maximize efficiency."
msgstr "UNIX(R) shell 不只是命令解释器，它还是一种强大的工具，允许用户执行命令、重定向命令的输出和输入，以及将命令串联起来以改进最终输出。结合内置命令使用这些功能，可以为用户提供一个能够最大限度提高效率的环境。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1798
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Shell redirection is the action of sending the output or the input of a "
"command into another command or into a file.  To capture the output of the "
"man:ls[1] command, for example, into a file, redirect the output:"
msgstr "Shell 重定向是将命令的输入或输出发送到另一个命令或文件的操作。例如，要将 man:ls[1] 命令的输出保存到文件中，可以重定向其输出："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1802
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% ls > directory_listing.txt\n"
msgstr "% ls > directory_listing.txt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1807
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The directory contents will now be listed in `directory_listing.txt`.  Some "
"commands can be used to read input, such as man:sort[1].  To sort this "
"listing, redirect the input:"
msgstr "现在，目录内容会列在 `directory_listing.txt` 中。有些命令可以读取输入，例如 man:sort[1]。要对该列表排序，请重定向输入："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1811
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% sort < directory_listing.txt\n"
msgstr "% sort < directory_listing.txt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1815
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The input will be sorted and placed on the screen.  To redirect that input "
"into another file, one could redirect the output of man:sort[1] by mixing "
"the direction:"
msgstr "输入会被排序并显示在屏幕上。要将该输入重定向到另一个文件，可以同时重定向 man:sort[1] 的输出："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1819
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% sort < directory_listing.txt > sorted.txt\n"
msgstr "% sort < directory_listing.txt > sorted.txt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1827
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In all of the previous examples, the commands are performing redirection "
"using file descriptors.  Every UNIX(R) system has file descriptors, which "
"include standard input (stdin), standard output (stdout), and standard error "
"(stderr).  Each one has a purpose, where input could be a keyboard or a "
"mouse, something that provides input.  Output could be a screen or paper in "
"a printer.  And error would be anything that is used for diagnostic or error "
"messages.  All three are considered I/O based file descriptors and sometimes "
"considered streams."
msgstr "在前面的所有示例中，命令都通过文件描述符执行重定向。每个 UNIX(R) 系统都有文件描述符，包括标准输入（stdin）、标准输出（stdout）和标准错误（stderr）。每种文件描述符都有其用途：输入可以来自键盘或鼠标等输入设备；输出可以显示在屏幕上，也可以打印在纸上；错误则用于诊断或错误消息。这三者都属于基于 I/O 的文件描述符，有时也称为数据流。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1830
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Through the use of these descriptors, the shell allows output and input "
#| "to be passed around through various commands and redirected to or from a "
#| "file. Another method of redirection is the pipe operator."
msgid ""
"Through the use of these descriptors, the shell allows output and input to "
"be passed around through various commands and redirected to or from a file.  "
"Another method of redirection is the pipe operator."
msgstr ""
"透过使用这些文件描述符，Shell能够让输出与输入在各种指令间传递与重新导向到或自"
"文件。另一种重新导向的方式是使用管线运算子（Pipe operator）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1833
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The UNIX(R) pipe operator, \"|\" allows the output of one command to be "
"directly passed or directed to another program.  Basically, a pipe allows "
"the standard output of a command to be passed as standard input to another "
"command, for example:"
msgstr "UNIX(R) 管道运算符“|”允许将一个命令的输出直接传递或导向另一个程序。简单来说，管道允许将一个命令的标准输出作为另一个命令的标准输入，例如："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1837
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% cat directory_listing.txt | sort | less\n"
msgstr "% cat directory_listing.txt | sort | less\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1841
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In that example, the contents of `directory_listing.txt` will be sorted and "
"the output passed to man:less[1].  This allows the user to scroll through "
"the output at their own pace and prevent it from scrolling off the screen."
msgstr "在此示例中，`directory_listing.txt` 的内容会经过排序，然后将输出传递给 man:less[1]。这样用户就可以按自己的节奏滚动查看输出，避免内容滚动出屏幕。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1843
#, no-wrap
msgid "Text Editors"
msgstr "文本编辑器"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1847
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most FreeBSD configuration is done by editing text files, so it is a good "
"idea to become familiar with a text editor.  FreeBSD comes with a few as "
"part of the base system, and many more are available in the Ports Collection."
msgstr ""
"FreeBSD 的很多配置都可以通过编辑文本文件来完成。 因此， 最好能熟悉某种文本编"
"辑器。 FreeBSD 基本系统中提供了一些， 您也可以从 Ports Collection 安装其它编"
"辑器。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1854
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A simple editor to learn is man:ee[1], which stands for easy editor.  To "
"start this editor, type `ee _filename_` where _filename_ is the name of the "
"file to be edited.  Once inside the editor, all of the commands for "
"manipulating the editor's functions are listed at the top of the display.  "
"The caret (`^`) represents kbd:[Ctrl], so `^e` expands to kbd:[Ctrl+e].  To "
"leave man:ee[1], press kbd:[Esc], then choose the \"leave editor\" option "
"from the main menu.  The editor will prompt to save any changes if the file "
"has been modified."
msgstr "适合入门学习的简单编辑器是 man:ee[1]，它是 easy editor（简易编辑器）的缩写。要启动此编辑器，请输入 `ee _filename_`，其中 __filename__ 是要编辑的文件名。进入编辑器后，屏幕顶部会列出用于操作编辑器功能的所有命令。插入符号（`^`）表示 kbd:[Ctrl]，因此 `^e` 等同于 kbd:[Ctrl+e]。要退出 man:ee[1]，请按 kbd:[Esc]，然后从主菜单中选择“leave editor”（退出编辑器）。如果文件已修改，编辑器会提示保存更改。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1859
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD also comes with more powerful text editors, such as man:vi[1], as "
"part of the base system.  Other editors, like package:editors/emacs[] and "
"package:editors/vim[], are part of the FreeBSD Ports Collection.  These "
"editors offer more functionality at the expense of being more complicated to "
"learn.  Learning a more powerful editor such as vim or Emacs can save more "
"time in the long run."
msgstr "FreeBSD 的基本系统还附带了功能更强大的文本编辑器，例如 man:vi[1]。其他编辑器，如 package:editors/emacs[] 和 package:editors/vim[]，则属于 FreeBSD Ports Collection。这些编辑器功能更多，但学习起来也更复杂。从长远来看，学习使用 vim 或 Emacs 这样的强大编辑器可以节省更多时间。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1863
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Many applications which modify files or require typed input will "
"automatically open a text editor.  To change the default editor, set the "
"`EDITOR` environment variable as described in crossref:basics[shells, "
"Shells]."
msgstr "许多会修改文件或需要输入文本的应用程序都会自动打开文本编辑器。要更改默认编辑器，请按照 crossref:basics[shells, Shells] 中的说明设置 `EDITOR` 环境变量。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1865
#, no-wrap
msgid "Devices and Device Nodes"
msgstr "设备和设备节点"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1870
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A device is a term used mostly for hardware-related activities in a system, "
"including disks, printers, graphics cards, and keyboards.  When FreeBSD "
"boots, the majority of the boot messages refer to devices being detected.  A "
"copy of the boot messages is saved to `/var/run/dmesg.boot`."
msgstr ""
"在一个系统里，硬件描述通常用法就是一个设备对应一个术语，包括磁盘、打印机、显"
"卡和键盘。 当 FreeBSD 启动过程中，大多数的设备都能探测到并显示出来， 您也可以"
"查阅<filename>/var/run/dmesg.boot</filename>， 引导时所有信息都在里面。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1873
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Each device has a device name and number.  For example, `ada0` is the first "
"SATA hard drive, while `kbd0` represents the keyboard."
msgstr ""
"每个设备都有设备名和编号，比如 <filename>ada0</filename> 代表第一个 SATA 硬"
"盘。<filename>kbd0</filename> 代表键盘。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1875
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most devices in FreeBSD must be accessed through special files called device "
"nodes, which are located in `/dev`."
msgstr ""
"在 FreeBSD 操作系统里，大多数设备存在的特殊访问文件就是叫做设备节点， 他们都"
"定位在<filename>/dev</filename>目录里。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1877
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual Pages"
msgstr "手册页"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1882
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The most comprehensive documentation on FreeBSD is in the form of manual "
"pages.  Nearly every program on the system comes with a short reference "
"manual explaining the basic operation and available arguments.  These "
"manuals can be viewed using `man`:"
msgstr ""
"最详细的使用说明文档莫过于 FreeBSD 里的联机手册了。 几乎每一个程序都会附上一"
"份简短说明， 以介绍这个程序的的基本功能以及参数的用法。 我们能通过 "
"<command>man</command> 命令来阅读这些说明， 而使用 <command>man</command> 命"
"令却是简单的事情:"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1886
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% man command\n"
msgstr "% man command\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1890
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"where _command_ is the name of the command to learn about.  For example, to "
"learn more about man:ls[1], type:"
msgstr "其中 _command_ 是要了解的命令名称。例如，要进一步了解 man:ls[1]，请输入："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1894
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% man ls\n"
msgstr "% man ls\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1898
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Manual pages are divided into sections which represent the type of topic. "
#| "In FreeBSD, the following sections are available:"
msgid ""
"Manual pages are divided into sections which represent the type of topic.  "
"In FreeBSD, the following sections are available:"
msgstr "这些在线手册分下列章节:"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1900
msgid "User commands."
msgstr "用户命令。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1901
msgid "System calls and error numbers."
msgstr "系统调用以及错误代码。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1902
msgid "Functions in the C libraries."
msgstr "C 库文件里的函数说明。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1903
msgid "Device drivers."
msgstr "设备驱动。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1904
msgid "File formats."
msgstr "文件格式。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1905
msgid "Games and other diversions."
msgstr "游戏以及其他娱乐。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1906
msgid "Miscellaneous information."
msgstr "各种资讯。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1907
msgid "System maintenance and operation commands."
msgstr "系统维护以及命令。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1908
msgid "System kernel interfaces."
msgstr "系统内核接口。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1912
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In some cases, the same topic may appear in more than one section of the "
"online manual.  For example, there is a `chmod` user command and a `chmod()` "
"system call.  To tell man:man[1] which section to display, specify the "
"section number:"
msgstr "在某些情况下，同一主题可能会出现在联机手册的多个章节中。例如，有一个名为 `chmod` 的用户命令，也有一个 `chmod()` 系统调用。要指定 man:man[1] 应显示的章节，请提供章节编号："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1916
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% man 1 chmod\n"
msgstr "% man 1 chmod\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1920
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This will display the manual page for the user command man:chmod[1].  "
"References to a particular section of the online manual are traditionally "
"placed in parenthesis in written documentation, so man:chmod[1] refers to "
"the user command and man:chmod[2] refers to the system call."
msgstr "这会显示用户命令 man:chmod[1] 的手册页。在书面文档中，通常用括号标注联机手册的特定章节，因此 man:chmod[1] 指用户命令，而 man:chmod[2] 指系统调用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1922
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the name of the manual page is unknown, use `man -k` to search for "
"keywords in the manual page descriptions:"
msgstr "如果不知道手册页名称，可以使用 `man -k` 按关键词搜索手册页说明："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1926
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% man -k mail\n"
msgstr "% man -k mail\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1930
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This command displays a list of commands that have the keyword \"mail\" in "
"their descriptions.  This is equivalent to using man:apropos[1]."
msgstr "此命令会显示说明中包含关键词“mail”的命令列表。这等效于使用 man:apropos[1]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1932
#, fuzzy
msgid "To read the descriptions for all of the commands in `/usr/sbin`, type:"
msgstr ""
"有时您会看到<filename>/usr/bin</filename> 下有许多命令但不知他们的用途， 您只"
"需这样做:"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1937
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% cd /usr/sbin\n"
"% man -f * | more\n"
msgstr "% cd /usr/sbin\n% man -f * | more\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1940
msgid "or"
msgstr "或"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1945
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% cd /usr/sbin\n"
"% whatis * |more\n"
msgstr "% cd /usr/sbin\n% whatis * |more\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1948
#, no-wrap
msgid "GNU Info Files"
msgstr "GNU Info 文件"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1953
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD includes several applications and utilities produced by the Free "
"Software Foundation (FSF).  In addition to manual pages, these programs may "
"include hypertext documents called `info` files.  These can be viewed using "
"man:info[1] or, if package:editors/emacs[] is installed, the info mode of "
"emacs."
msgstr "FreeBSD 包含自由软件基金会（FSF）开发的多个应用程序和实用程序。除了手册页外，这些程序还可能包含称为 `info` 文件的超文本文档。可以使用 man:info[1] 查看这些文档；如果已安装 package:editors/emacs[]，也可以使用 emacs 的 info 模式查看。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1955
#, fuzzy
msgid "To use man:info[1], type:"
msgstr "要使用 man:info[1]，请输入："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1959
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% info\n"
msgstr "% info\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/basics/_index.adoc:1962
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
